  "goodToKnow": "Hierdurch means through this or as a result of this: Hierdurch verringert sich der Aufwand. It refers back to something just mentioned and is typical of formal and technical writing, manuals and official letters. In speech, Germans say dadurch. It belongs to the hier- family: hiermit (herewith), hiervon (of this), hierfür (for this), hierzu (in addition to this). Using these makes your writing sound precise but bureaucratic."
